High Availability (HA) and Disaster Recovery (DR) in Kubernetes
________________________________________
1. High Availability (HA)
Definition:
Ensures applications remain available even if some components fail.
Key Areas & Approaches:
1.	Control Plane HA
o	Multi-master API servers, controller managers, schedulers.
o	etcd cluster with odd number of nodes (3, 5, 7) for quorum.
o	Spread across multiple availability zones (AZs).
2.	Node & Pod HA
o	Deploy multiple replicas using Deployments (stateless) or StatefulSets (stateful).
o	Spread pods across nodes/AZs using:
	Node Affinity / Anti-Affinity
	Pod Affinity / Anti-Affinity
o	Use taints/tolerations for dedicated critical workloads.
3.	Load Balancing
o	Use Ingress + LoadBalancer to distribute traffic across pods.
o	Ensures HA at request level.
4.	Database HA
o	Use replication:
	MySQL: Master-Slave or Group Replication
	PostgreSQL: Streaming replication
	MongoDB: Replica Set
o	Deploy database pods across different nodes or zones.
________________________________________
2. Disaster Recovery (DR)
Definition:
Ensures recovery from catastrophic failures (e.g., AZ outage, cluster loss, data corruption).
Key Approaches:
1.	Backups
o	Regularly backup etcd and persistent volumes (PVs).
o	Use tools like Velero, Kasten, or Stash.
2.	Multi-Region / Multi-Cluster
o	Deploy a secondary cluster in another region.
o	Replicate critical data to prevent data loss.
3.	Restore Testing
o	Test failure scenarios: node loss, AZ outage, etcd corruption.
o	Verify pods and data recovery.
4.	Stateless Applications
o	Simple redeploy to another cluster or region; no data migration needed.
5.	Stateful Applications
o	Use PVs, replication, offsite backups.
o	Automate restoration processes.
________________________________________
3. Best Practices Summary
Area	Approach
Control Plane	Multi-master, etcd cluster, spread across AZs
Nodes & Pods	Multiple replicas, spread across nodes/AZs, use affinity/anti-affinity
Load Balancing	Ingress / Service LoadBalancer for traffic distribution
Databases	Replication, failover, cross-AZ deployment, persistent volume backups
Backups	Regular etcd + PV backups, automated tools
Disaster Recovery	Secondary cluster/region, DR runbooks, restore testing
Stateless Apps	Redeploy as needed
Stateful Apps	Persistent storage, replication, offsite backups
________________________________________
Interview-Ready One-Liner
For HA, deploy multiple replicas across nodes/AZs with load balancing and database replication. For DR, backup etcd and persistent volumes, replicate data to another cluster or region, and test restoration regularly.

